WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.905
Understanding your compliance requirements is an important part of selling on Amazon.

00:00:04.905 --> 00:00:11.037
Products that meet all applicable laws and regulations keep your customers safe from health and

00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:11.854
safety risks.

00:00:11.854 --> 00:00:16.351
Failure to meet these regulations may negatively impact your account health.

00:00:16.351 --> 00:00:22.891
Your inventory at Amazon's fulfillment centers could be disposed of or stopped at customs if you

00:00:22.891 --> 00:00:23.708
ship internationally.

00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:29.022
You might not receive your payments and your product listing may be removed.

00:00:29.022 --> 00:00:29.840
Most importantly,

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.945
you may lose your ability to add new products.

00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:35.360
To avoid these penalties and stay compliant,

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.400
use the Compliance Knowledge Portal to check your compliance requirements proactively before listing

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.063
your product.

00:00:41.063 --> 00:00:45.040
This gives you the time to obtain necessary documents or test reports

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.640
and ensure your product and listing meet compliance requirements,

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.040
preventing your product listing from being removed, inventory being disposed of,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.566
or even account deactivation.

00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:58.000
Make sure to check all the requirements including laws,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
regulations, and standards, required compliance documents, and requirements for images and product

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:04.800
listing details.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.200
You can download these requirements for easy reference throughout your compliance

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:15.120
journey from the initial research and pre-listing stage through product listing and labeling to

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.065
managing any policy violations.

00:01:17.065 --> 00:01:21.440
Regulations can change periodically, so it's important to verify

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.942
current requirements before listing.

00:01:22.942 --> 00:01:26.320
If your product is flagged for compliance after listing,

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:31.840
you will receive an email notification prompting you to review and address any unmet requirements.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.800
You can also find these notifications in your account health dashboard under the policy compliance

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:37.237
section.

00:01:37.237 --> 00:01:42.480
Address each notification by submitting the correct documentation or submitting an appeal

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.840
if you believe your product was flagged incorrectly.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.200
Refer to the compliance help pages for additional

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.880
guidance as requirements can vary based on product attributes like size, intended use,

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.309
or target age group.

00:01:54.309 --> 00:01:58.240
If you can't find your specific product, start by reviewing requirements

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.053
for similar product types.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:03.680
Avoid keywords that might trigger incorrect product classification

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.144
unless they accurately describe your product.

00:02:06.144 --> 00:02:09.840
For example, don't use for kids or toy unless

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.048
your product is intended for children.

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:15.360
If you have questions, contact seller support with specific

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.391
details about your product before listing.

00:02:17.391 --> 00:02:19.760
The compliance knowledge portal also includes a

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.131
directory of service providers to obtain the documentation you need.

00:02:23.131 --> 00:02:24.480
You can select providers

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.269
based on location if you source from overseas.

00:02:27.269 --> 00:02:29.360
When you expand your business globally,

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.840
check for compliance requirements in that region as you won't be able to launch your product in

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.550
stores where your product is prohibited.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.400
Use these tips to help you stay compliant and keep

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:45.360
your products available to customers.
